factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The reel_script says the rainwater tanks in Pollachi are 'பராமரிக்கப்படாமல் பயன்பாடின்றி உள்ளன' (unmaintained and unused) in many places; the article says tanks became unused due to non-implementation and non-maintenance over time, which is roughly consistent, but the phrase 'பல இடங்களில்' (in many places) is an overstatement not stated in the article.
  The reel_script says 'ஆறு குழுக்கள் அமைக்கப்பட்டுள்ளன' for inspecting government buildings and then states the inspection of 'நகராட்சி கட்டடங்கள், பஸ் ஸ்டாண்ட், ஆரம்ப சுகாதார நிலையங்கள், வணிக வளாகங்கள், அரசு கட்டடங்கள்' - the article says a committee of officials was formed (ஆறு குழுக்கள் - six groups) only for the inspection, so the wording 'அதிகாரிகள் அடங்கிய குழு' plus 'ஆறு குழுக்கள்' is consistent, but the reel_script's claim that 'ஆறு குழுக்கள் அறிக்கை அளிக்க வேண்டும்' is fine; no issue here.
  The reel_script omits that the commissioner's meeting with engineers and registered engineers was held and that the decision was taken at that meeting, and omits the fact that the tanks were rendered unused because of lack of maintenance is included, but the key fact that the meeting was chaired by the commissioner is not an important omission.
  The caption's 'Pollachi rainwater harvesting 30 days | Coimbatore news' and date are footer-type content and are excluded from checking.
